n no way  home i mean really this is like the  biggest movie that everybody's been  talking about all year long we surveyed  thousands of movie fans heading into  december and spider-man no way home is  the most anticipated film according to  moviegoers and according to me what does  it lead to what else does it open up in  terms of the future of the spider-man  universe a lot of questions still need  to be answered yeah and the trailer is  trickling out even more questions all  along the way that last one was  incredible exactly yes it was you know  and what people should know about this  film in case there's questions peter  parker's identity was revealed at the  end of the last film and so everyone now  knows who he is it's causing disarray in  his life but when he asks dr strange to  cast a spell so that everyone forgets  he's spider-man it opens up this monster  can of worms that involves a crack in  the multiverse that allows spider-man's  greatest foes to return to exact revenge  upon him and so a lot of people are  excited because they're bringing back  villains from previous spider-man films  that starred toby maguire and andrew  garfield and of course a lot of people  are expecting at some point to see those  two as well return and be with tom  holland spider-man and so i think  there's a lot of anticipation for this  kind of film because it is a monster  crossover movie not just with characters  that are currently existing in other  movies but characters we haven't seen  for like over a decade i think that's  cool i'm really looking forward to just  turning into a child in the movie  theaters okay so every year my family we  always go to see a movie so what do you  think would be a fun movie for the whole  family to watch this year i think  there's a couple you know if you have  really young kids i'm going to say sing  too that is a sequel to sing and what i  love about it especially if the words  kids bop mean something to you in your  house  you are going to want to go see sing too  because it's littered with music that is  familiar to kids that's music that's on  the radio now like these cover versions  of the songs and it's got such a great  cast scarlett johansson reese  witherspoon tori kelly john c riley  matthew mcconaughey and they all play  these really great animal characters and  there's always themes in there about  believing in yourself and believing in  your talents and so i think that is a  really great film for little kids but  there's another film with a lot of music  in it and it has a very famous director  attached steven spielberg has a remake  of west side story that just looks  outstanding and gorgeous so i think if  you have some older kids that are also  really like music maybe they didn't see  the original west side story maybe they  didn't see it on broadway as a musical  but this new version is something that i  think a lot of people will really wrap  their arms around plus rita moreno who  was a star in the original west side  story returns and has a role in this one  and so i think that's going to be a film  that a lot of people are talking about  and may even be an awards contender as  well as we get closer to the holidays do  you think there are any other december  movies that could become oscar winners  yeah i mean we could definitely see a  couple in december you know they've been  rolling out over the last couple of  months but there's one from director  guillermo del toro called nightmare  alley that i want to put on everyone's  radar last film that guillermo del toro  directed won best picture and best  director and so i think that he's  somebody that a lot of people are  exciting right now about bradley cooper  stars rooney mara cate blanchett kind of  a remake of a 1947 film also called  nightmare alley and it's about a corrupt  con man who teams up with a female  psychiatrist to trick people into giving  them money i personally love con man  stories and i think with guillermo 